# Change Safety and Approval Gate

- Never remove, hide, or degrade any UI element or user-facing functionality unless the user explicitly approves that specific change.
- If a request is ambiguous, ask a clarifying question before making UI/feature removals.
- Before implementing non-trivial code changes, perform a short impact assessment covering:
  - affected modules/files
  - expected behavior changes
  - regression risk level
- Present the impact assessment clearly and obtain user confirmation before proceeding with impactful changes.
- Preserve existing behavior by default; prefer minimal, reversible changes.
- When requested changes could affect existing flows, include a brief validation plan (build/test/runtime checks) before implementation.
